 "src": "Flipkart Data Engineer OA (IIT BHU)",
 "body": "<p>You are given a word. Sort its letters alphabetically to get the <em>sorted word</em>.</p><p>Match each letter of the original word to the same letter in the sorted word. Repeated letters are matched in order of appearance: the first <code>a</code> of the word goes with the first <code>a</code> of the sorted word, and so on. Positions are 0-indexed.</p><p>For every letter of the original word, compute <code>v = |original position − sorted position| + ASCII(last letter of the sorted word)</code> and take the digit sum of <code>v</code>. Add these digit sums together to get <code>X</code>.</p><p>Finally take the digit sum of <code>X</code> once (do not repeat) and turn it into a letter: 1 → A, 2 → B, …, 26 → Z, 27 → A again, and so on.</p><p>Print <code>X</code> and the letter.</p>",
 "inp": "One line with the word.",
 "out": "<code>X</code> and the letter, separated by a space.",
